        <OtherAbstract Type="PIP" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>Treatment regimens for dysmenorrhea are discussed. Oral contraceptives are the best method for overcoming dysmenorrhea. If these do not work or if there are contraindications or adversion to oral contraceptive use, analgesics can be used (e.g. naproxin, dolemone, bellergal). Prostaglandin inhibitors such as naprosyn can help treat dysmenorrhea. Cervical dilatation is an old but still used treatment for dysmenorrhea. In severe cases the nervus praesacralis is severed or, in extreme cases, hysterectomy is performed.</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
